1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,470
Meet HybridPay — a universal fiat and crypto payment terminal.

2
00:00:10,470 --> 00:00:17,250
Fiat rails, crypto wallets, and programmable money live in separate tools with separate rules.

3
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:26,270
HybridPay unifies them in one sandbox, where deterministic backend rules authorize every movement, and everything is audited.

4
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:35,490
The Banking Workspace is the operator's control plane: live KPIs, programmable contracts, disputes, and an admin-gated panel.

5
00:00:35,490 --> 00:00:42,270
Operators read and monitor; money movement needs an admin token plus maker-checker approval.

6
00:00:42,270 --> 00:00:48,890
In the Personal Workspace I sign in with an operator token that lives only in browser memory.

7
00:00:48,890 --> 00:00:53,090
Then I send one thousand minor units: create, then confirm.

8
00:00:53,090 --> 00:01:02,840
The backend provider decides, never the frontend — and the result comes back authorized, with a payment identifier and a sandbox receipt.

9
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:13,370
The simulator proves failures are first-class: a declined payment returns a structured provider decline — scenario passed, payment declined.

10
00:01:13,370 --> 00:01:15,850
Timeouts stay honestly ambiguous.

11
00:01:15,850 --> 00:01:20,510
A decline is an expected business outcome, and a passing test.

12
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:27,380
Money with conditions: a plain-words agreement becomes a validated programmable contract.

13
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:33,330
Guardrails never sleep — unknown categories rejected, wrong networks refused.

14
00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:38,740
And no AI recommendation can bypass deterministic authorization rules.

15
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:45,160
At the center is the Meta Muse Spark integration — it advises only, never authorizes.

16
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:48,410
Every answer arrives labeled advisory-only.

17
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:55,520
Here it runs as a transparent sandbox stub, while real keys stay server-side in Modal Secrets.

18
00:01:55,520 --> 00:02:01,870
Policy first, AI second — approval always stands between a suggestion and any funds.

19
00:02:01,870 --> 00:02:11,800
History is tenant-isolated and searchable, with downloadable sandbox receipts for every record — the audit trail behind every payment state.

20
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:21,910
Security is architecture: role-based access, independent policy enforcement, idempotency keys, human approvals, tenant isolation.

21
00:02:21,910 --> 00:02:26,070
The Private Workspace mirrors the same sign-in model.

22
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:35,200
Receiving is Sepolia-only: a tracked request is created, and your own wallet signs — the terminal never sees keys.

23
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:38,970
Sandbox today, trusted infrastructure tomorrow.
